question:
Let f₁: R → R, f₂: [0, ∞) → R, f₃: R → R and f₄: R → [0, ∞) be defined by
f₁(x) = |x| if x < 0; eˣ if x ≥ 0;
f₂(x) = x²;
f₃(x) = sin x if x < 0; x if x ≥ 0;
and f₄(x) = f₂(f₁(x)) if x < 0; f₂(f₁(x)) – 1 if x ≥ 0
List I: P. f₄ is, Q. f₃ is, R. f₂ o f₁ is, S. f₂ is
List II: 1. onto but not one-one, 2. neither continuous nor one-one, 3. differentiable but not one-one, 4. continuous and one-one [JEE (Advanced) 2014, Paper-2, (3, –1)/60]
